#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111839 :tutorial/content "We categorize angles that are not right, straight, or full into three groups.\n\n- An **acute angle** has a measure between $0^\\circ$ and $90^\\circ$:![](images/ec/ec35031af65d0ea9e08121d3df02ed136c5b81b2f90698f4a51681657e67de48.png)\n- An **obtuse angle** has a measure between $90^\\circ$ and $180^\\circ$:![](images/a9/a96bdfed918f56e7f5cc1cfe9eaad42dcd32a54e663c78fead08e68e6ef80865.png)\n\n- Angles whose measure is between $180^\\circ$ and $360^\\circ$ are called **reflex angles**.![](images/62/62323a85f8b3357628c2d221f0293c94ec4c3d9e6e8d1ca65400d2ea7349d3ce.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "e1cb4bf7-16f7-5ca9-9702-5ecd2112e696" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2180 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
